WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.475
A baker came out of his shop and stared at the boys.

2
00:00:04.476 --> 00:00:09.342
"Edward, you’d better get back to the tailor shop," said the baker.

3
00:00:09.343 --> 00:00:12.280
"Your master will be angry."

4
00:00:12.281 --> 00:00:15.417
"I don’t care," said Edward.

5
00:00:15.418 --> 00:00:17.747
"I was born for the stage.

6
00:00:17.748 --> 00:00:22.006
I don’t want to be a tailor!"

7
00:00:22.007 --> 00:00:25.536
"Are you a tailor?’ asked Vinnie.

8
00:00:25.537 --> 00:00:30.291
"No, I am an apprentice," said Edward.

9
00:00:30.292 --> 00:00:33.537
"Apprentice?" asked Vinnie.

10
00:00:33.538 --> 00:00:39.008
"Young boys need to learn skills for different jobs," said Edward.

11
00:00:39.009 --> 00:00:43.148
"My master, the tailor, is teaching me to sew."

12
00:00:43.149 --> 00:00:47.004
"Do you like making clothes?" asked Vinnie.

13
00:00:47.005 --> 00:00:50.340
"It’s all right," said Edward.

14
00:00:50.341 --> 00:00:54.128
"But my talent is wasted sewing shirts and coats.

15
00:00:54.129 --> 00:00:56.213
I’m an actor!"

16
00:00:56.214 --> 00:01:00.801
"Really?" said Vinnie, impressed.

17
00:01:00.802 --> 00:01:05.276
"Where do you work?" Edward asked Vinnie.

18
00:01:05.277 --> 00:01:09.386
"Oh, I’m not an apprentice," said Vinnie.

19
00:01:09.387 --> 00:01:11.011
"I go to school."

20
00:01:11.012 --> 00:01:14.877
"You are very lucky," said Edward.

21
00:01:14.878 --> 00:01:19.758
"My family is poor, so I must live with the tailor."

22
00:01:19.759 --> 00:01:26.876
Suddenly, the boys heard a man calling angrily, "Edward! Where are you?"

23
00:01:26.877 --> 00:01:31.624
"That is my master," sighed Edward.

24
00:01:31.625 --> 00:01:33.342
"I have to go, Vinnie.

25
00:01:33.343 --> 00:01:35.142
I can’t practice now.

26
00:01:35.143 --> 00:01:39.830
But someday the queen will see my great talent!"

27
00:01:39.831 --> 00:01:42.889
"What queen?" asked Vinnie.

28
00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:47.809
"Why, Queen Elizabeth of England!" cried Edward.

29
00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:52.431
"Queen Elizabeth?" Vinnie scratched his head.

30
00:01:52.432 --> 00:01:56.758
"Isn’t she the queen of England now? " he

31
00:01:56.759 --> 00:02:00.069
thought. Mandy might be able to explain it to

32
00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:03.008
him. But where was his

33
00:02:03.009 --> 00:02:06.608
sister? Meanwhile, Mandy felt like

34
00:02:06.609 --> 00:02:10.817
crying. "How did we get separated?" she wondered.

35
00:02:10.818 --> 00:02:13.238
"Now I’m all alone.

36
00:02:13.239 --> 00:02:15.884
How will I get home?"

37
00:02:15.885 --> 00:02:19.733
She lifted her skirt to check her scraped knee.

38
00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:23.508
A carriage drove up alongside Mandy.

39
00:02:23.509 --> 00:02:27.413
A woman wearing a fancy hat looked out.

40
00:02:27.414 --> 00:02:31.016
"Are you all right?" she asked Mandy.

41
00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:34.009
"Oh, you’re bleeding!"

42
00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:39.142
"It’s okay," Mandy said, sniffing.

43
00:02:39.143 --> 00:02:42.881
"Where do you live?" asked the woman.

44
00:02:42.882 --> 00:02:46.341
Mandy bowed her head and didn’t answer.

45
00:02:46.342 --> 00:02:48.813
"Let me clean up your knee.

46
00:02:48.814 --> 00:02:53.015
Charles will take you home later," said the woman.

47
00:02:53.016 --> 00:02:56.479
Undecided, Mandy paused for a moment.

48
00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:02.468
"Charles," she said to the driver, "open the door for the little girl."

49
00:03:02.469 --> 00:03:06.342
"Yes, Lady Katherine," replied the driver.

50
00:03:06.343 --> 00:03:11.492
Mandy stared at the woman and then got into the carriage.

51
00:03:11.493 --> 00:03:15.816
"She must be very rich!" she thought.

52
00:03:15.817 --> 00:03:18.824
"I wish Vinnie could meet her!"

53
00:03:18.825 --> 00:03:23.680
However, Vinnie was seeing a different side of London.

54
00:03:23.681 --> 00:03:27.280
Vinnie and Edward arrived at the tailor shop.

55
00:03:27.281 --> 00:03:33.501
Master Crossland, the tailor, was standing in the door with his hands on his hips.

56
00:03:33.502 --> 00:03:36.824
"So you’re hanging out with actors again!"

57
00:03:36.825 --> 00:03:39.880
said the tailor, looking at Vinnie.

58
00:03:39.881 --> 00:03:43.608
"I’m not an actor, sir," said Vinnie.

59
00:03:43.609 --> 00:03:48.487
"In that case, you are welcome, young man," said the tailor.

60
00:03:48.488 --> 00:03:51.487
"Come, it’s one o’clock and time to eat.

61
00:03:51.488 --> 00:03:55.667
After lunch, maybe you can help Edward with his work."

62
00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:59.467
The tailor then turned to Edward and said,

63
00:03:59.468 --> 00:04:06.459
"When will you stop dreaming of Shakespeare?"

